{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions","id":914866,"title":"Stupid Spirit Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T09:22:19-07:00","id":914866,"title":"Stupid Spirit Questions","content":"I'm working on a spirit cataloging chronicle, and I have a few questions about the extent of the things which there can be spirits of. Are there spirits of spirits? Spirits of vampires? Mages? I might have missed something, but it looks like spirits are usually of nouns, but how far does that go? There are car spirits which cause accidents, are but &quot;car accident&quot; is also a thing, so are there independent spirits of car accidents who haunt roadways? Are there potentially spirits of ghosts of car accident victims?<br /> <br /> I know this ultimately depends on the chronicle, but is there any guidance from the line as a whole? I have the 2nd Edition core book, but I'm hardly fluent in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11956-miscellany","name":"Miscellany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T09:35:41-07:00","id":914875,"title":"","content":"1) Arguably? Idigam and/or Pangaeans;<br /> <br /> 2) There's a Cru\u00e1c ritual for those;<br /> <br /> 3) Ghost mages count? If not, there's a legacy that slowly warp themselves into such;<br /> <br /> 4) A conceptual spirit of car accidents? Possible, but it wouldn't be long lived;<br /> <br /> 5) Spirits that are capable of eating ghosts are known to incorporating traits of their victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T09:38:32-07:00","id":914876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miscellany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions#post914866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there spirits of spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you count the idigam as proper spirits, and then only as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits of vampires? Mages? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there potentially spirits of ghosts of car accident victims? </div> </div> </div>Ex-humans are generally subject to the same stipulation as humans re: no direct spiritual reflection. Ditto things that are &quot;native&quot; to other realms of existence like the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I might have missed something, but it looks like spirits are usually of nouns, but how far does that go? There are car spirits which cause accidents, are but &quot;car accident&quot; is also a thing, so are there independent spirits of car accidents who haunt roadways? </div> </div> </div>At the most basic level, spirits correspond to resonance. What a spirit is &quot;a spirit of&quot; can shift over time as its portfolio expands, but they tend to anchor on &quot;noun&quot; phenomena, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T09:38:56-07:00","id":914877,"title":"","content":"There's spirits of everything except humans, so a noun except for the person part. So, yes, there's car spirits, car accident spirits, accident spirits, murder car spirits, roadkill spirits. Car accident spirits would probably be easier to catalog under accidents in general just so you don't get ultra-specific, which can hamper games. There are spirits of 'the dead,' mostly made up of the act and the memories of the victim that can seem like a ghost, but isn't. You can also have magath which further expands the legions of spirits, where a car spirit may also be a sun spirit and a tree spirit.<br /> <br /> The Predators book really gets into spirits. It has a lot of them listed with descriptions and goes into the basics of their life-cycle.<br /> <br /> We've discussed the vampire thing and it's still undecided. I believe there would be, others don't as it's too close to human. There doesn't seem to be mage spirits, but there would be magic spirits. I don't believe there are spirits of spirits, as spirits don't exist in the 'real world' to offer a spiritual reflection of themselves, but there may be a spirit of spirituality or shamanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:44:45-07:00","id":914910,"title":"","content":"RE: Vampire spirits. I think there would certainly be spirits of parisitism, spirits of nocturnal predation, spirits of hemophagia, etc. A spirit could probably resonate with all of the above without getting into magath territory. Whether such a spirit could technically be considered a vampire spirit is pretty academic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:49:40-07:00","id":914912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=914910#post914910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Vampire spirits. I think there would certainly be spirits of parisitism, spirits of nocturnal predation, spirits of hemophagia, etc. A spirit could probably resonate with all of the above without getting into magath territory. Whether such a spirit could technically be considered a vampire spirit is pretty academic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strix might fit the bill too. Altho just in the general ephemeral entity sense and not strictly spiritually speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:57:38-07:00","id":914918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=914912#post914912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Strix might fit the bill too. Altho just in the general ephemeral entity sense and not strictly spiritually speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically Strix aren't even made of ephemera and don't have a Twilight frequency. But I do agree that they are the most direct &quot;spiritual&quot; counterpart to vampires, in a very broad sense of the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:04:32-07:00","id":914923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=914918#post914918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically Strix aren't even made of ephemera and don't have a Twilight frequency. But I do agree that they are the most direct &quot;spiritual&quot; counterpart to vampires, in a very broad sense of the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using the term ephemeral entity because they work off Power, Finesse &amp; Resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:56:56-07:00","id":915004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miscellany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions#post914866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a spirit cataloging chronicle, and I have a few questions about the extent of the things which there can be spirits of. Are there spirits of spirits? Spirits of vampires? Mages? I might have missed something, but it looks like spirits are usually of nouns, but how far does that go? There are car spirits which cause accidents, are but &quot;car accident&quot; is also a thing, so are there independent spirits of car accidents who haunt roadways? Are there potentially spirits of ghosts of car accident victims?<br /> <br /> I know this ultimately depends on the chronicle, but is there any guidance from the line as a whole? I have the 2nd Edition core book, but I'm hardly fluent in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try to read the whole thread here. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\"> A grab-bag of Shadow - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A lot of people have trouble visualising the Hisil, or coming up with ideas for how the Shadow representation of an area could appear. This is a thread to help fix that. (I don't recall a thread dealing with this before. If we have one, please point me towards it.) Here's the game - pick any place that you think is likely to be part of a territory and describe how it appears in the Hisil. Describe what it looks like, what spirits you find there, how they interact, and how they're likely to react to Uratha intruders. (This can be as broad or narrow as you like. A spirit ecology may respond well to </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:11:29-07:00","id":915020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=915004#post915004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try to read the whole thread here.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...f-shadow/page2</a></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11956-miscellany\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11956\" data-vbnamecard=\"11956\">Miscellany</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow\">Actual relevant link</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:45:29-07:00","id":915392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=914877#post914877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's spirits of everything except humans, so a noun except for the person part. So, yes, there's car spirits, car accident spirits, accident spirits, murder car spirits, roadkill spirits. Car accident spirits would probably be easier to catalog under accidents in general just so you don't get ultra-specific, which can hamper games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always envisioned that spirits Umia is based on most basic, broad description that can have many interpretation - there is car Umia, mammals Umia, weather Umia, emotions Umia. Too specific to be Choir ( like vehicles, animals, environments and thoughts ) but enough to form their own family in greater kinds. Then all our exampled 'car spirits' will be in 'Car Umia' and they will be different splints in it.<br /> <br /> What I have most basic advice to share - <b>Those spirits from the same Umia? They will have at least one dot of Influence in basic Umia phenomenon.</b> So car spirits, car accident spirits, accident spirits, murder car spirits, roadkill spirits - they all will have at least 1 dot in Influence: Cars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T22:01:02-07:00","id":915401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=915392#post915392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always envisioned that spirits Umia is based on most basic, broad description that can have many interpretation - there is car Umia, mammals Umia, weather Umia, emotions Umia. Too specific to be Choir ( like vehicles, animals, environments and thoughts ) but enough to form their own family in greater kinds. Then all our exampled 'car spirits' will be in 'Car Umia' and they will be different splints in it.<br /> <br /> What I have most basic advice to share - <b>Those spirits from the same Umia? They will have at least one dot of Influence in basic Umia phenomenon.</b> So car spirits, car accident spirits, accident spirits, murder car spirits, roadkill spirits - they all will have at least 1 dot in Influence: Cars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good rule. And the rest makes sense.<br /> <br /> Logically, I think, you would have more specific things. A grey squirrel and a red squirrel recognize the other as different, just as a human observer might. Red sports cars and grey sedan are going to elicit very different feelings in viewers. But from a game perspective, that would get ridiculous, and it's much easier to go for broad generalizations than hyper-specific differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T22:52:22-07:00","id":915416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914866-stupid-spirit-questions?p=915401#post915401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logically, I think, you would have more specific things. A grey squirrel and a red squirrel recognize the other as different, just as a human observer might. Red sports cars and grey sedan are going to elicit very different feelings in viewers. But from a game perspective, that would get ridiculous, and it's much easier to go for broad generalizations than hyper-specific differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of the spirits with same Influences as D&amp;D same Class characters - both are 'ax handling fighters of 10th level', but one is little blond girl with eye-patch after traumatic events that killed her family and second is seasoned dwarven veteran that defend his clan in mountains. Same rough build, totally different characters - but still both characters would of same Umia of 'fighter class'. Even more, they would have totally the same Influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:34:57-07:00","id":915627,"title":"","content":"This has all been really useful. Thank you very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11956-miscellany","name":"Miscellany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}